activity-date.narrative:
•	To improve value for money of GFATM spending through 31st March 2024 and beyond;
•	To increase access to diagnosis, prevention, and treatment commodities to end the epidemics of HIV, tuberculosis and malaria, and to accelerate attainment of the UN Sustainable Development Goals; 
•	To leverage GFATM’s leadership and purchase volumes to realise cost savings for other procurers in LMICs.
During the grant, MedAccess will seek FCDO support to cover the staff time required to develop propositions that are expected to improve access to HIV, TB, and malaria products and value-for-money for GFATM.
